# CODEOWNERS — review routing for sensitive paths. See operator docs in
# the private core repo.
#
# WHAT THIS ACTUALLY ENFORCES. @forge-cold is a hardware-2FA "cold" account
# held by the SAME person as @verastd. Listing both owners on a path is
# TWO-CREDENTIAL FRICTION, not two-person control: GitHub's code-owner
# requirement is satisfied when ANY ONE listed owner approves. Because GitHub
# does not count a PR author's own approval, a @verastd-authored change to these
# paths does force a sign-in to the cold account and its hardware key — real
# cost for a stolen hot-account session or token. It is not independent
# review, and it does not constrain a compromised or mistaken operator.
# Nothing here should be described as "two-person control" or "two-key".
#
# Upgrade path (Phase 1+, before sensitive-path changes become routine):
#   1. Add a second HUMAN maintainer — or a team with >= 2 human members — as
#      co-owner of the paths below.
#   2. Set required_approving_review_count to 2 in
#      .github/rulesets/main-protection.json.
#   3. Keep require_last_push_approval and dismiss_stale_reviews_on_push true
#      (already set) so an approval cannot survive a later push.
# Only with all three does "two independent approvals" become accurate.

*                                               @verastd

/.github/                                      @verastd @forge-cold
/CODEOWNERS                                    @verastd @forge-cold
/contracts/                                    @verastd @forge-cold
/apps/api/src/forge_api/routers/auth*          @verastd @forge-cold
/apps/api/src/forge_api/routers/pay*           @verastd @forge-cold
/packages/contracts-client/                    @verastd @forge-cold

# Sign-in with GitHub (FORGE v0.2 Phase 1, ADR-003): session sealing, the
# OAuth state/PKCE flow, and the BFF's Origin check and assertion minting.
/packages/auth/                                @verastd @forge-cold
/apps/web/src/app/auth/                        @verastd @forge-cold
/apps/web/src/app/bff/                         @verastd @forge-cold
/apps/web/src/middleware.ts                    @verastd @forge-cold
/apps/web/src/lib/session.ts                   @verastd @forge-cold
/apps/api/src/forge_api/services/identity.py   @verastd @forge-cold
/apps/web/src/lib/auth/                        @verastd @forge-cold
# The lobby's LiveKit room token: it signs whose voice and name tag a member is.
/apps/web/src/app/api/lobby/                   @verastd @forge-cold
# Whether practice sessions count at all: decided at build time by these two.
/apps/web/src/lib/mode.ts                      @verastd @forge-cold
/apps/web/next.config.mjs                      @verastd @forge-cold
# Secret-scan suppressions: a contributor PR must never silence the scan for itself.
/.gitleaksignore                               @verastd @forge-cold
# What coding agents load as instructions: a PR here rewrites every contributor's agent.
/AGENTS.md                                     @verastd @forge-cold
/CLAUDE.md                                     @verastd @forge-cold
/.gemini/                                      @verastd @forge-cold
